# SHEscale — Smart Scheme Matcher & Loan Application Generator (Analyzed & Enhanced Prompt)

> **Purpose of this document:** Your uploaded PDF was a solid standalone feature prompt, but it was written as if this feature exists in isolation. Since it's actually going INTO SHEscale, I analyzed it against your already-built database, backend structure, and frontend design system — and rewrote it so it plugs into what already exists instead of duplicating it.

---

## 🔍 Analysis — What Needed Fixing Before This Goes to the AI

| Issue in the original PDF | Why it's a problem for SHEscale | Fix applied below |
|---|---|---|
| Proposes new **`Scheme`** and **`UserApplication`** Mongoose models | You already have `GovernmentScheme.model.js` and `FundingApplication.model.js` in `models/`. Creating new ones duplicates data and breaks the single-source-of-truth RAG pipeline you already built for the Live Government Scheme Panel. | Reuse the **existing** `GovernmentScheme` and `FundingApplication` models — extend fields only if truly missing, don't fork new collections. |
| Proposes a **local `faiss-node` vector DB queried directly inside the controller** | Violates your own backend rule: controllers only orchestrate, business logic lives in `services/`. Also duplicates the RAG retrieval logic you already spec'd in `services/ragRetrievalService.js`. | Fold the similarity search into the **existing** `ragRetrievalService.js` (faiss-node as its retrieval engine), called from the controller — not built as a one-off. |
| No mention of the **shared Gemini service wrapper** | Original prompt calls the Gemini API directly from the route logic. You already spec'd a single `services/geminiService.js` for every Gemini call across the app. | Route both the scheme-matching call and the loan-application-generation call through `geminiService.js`. |
| UI styled with generic Tailwind, no color system referenced | You already locked in a white + `#F50A70` design token system for the entire platform. A feature built without referencing it will visually clash with everything else. | Explicitly bind every component to the existing design tokens, not raw Tailwind defaults. |
| No loading/empty/error state requirement | You already made this a hard rule for the whole frontend (no mocked data, real states only). The original prompt only mentions a spinner for the scan button. | Extend real loading/empty/error states to all 3 components, not just the input. |
| Component names (`IdeaInput`, `SchemeCards`, `ApplicationDraft`) exist in a vacuum | Your frontend prompt already named this feature's parent screen `SchemeMatcher.jsx`. These 3 components should nest under it, not float as a separate untethered feature. | Explicitly structure them as children of the existing `SchemeMatcher.jsx` screen. |
| "At least 3 schemes" is a hardcoded minimum | Your Live Government Scheme Intelligence Panel already keeps `GovernmentScheme` current — the match count should be however many genuinely qualify, not artificially padded to hit 3. | Loosen this to "as many as genuinely match, ranked by relevance" with 3 as a typical/expected range, not a forced floor. |

