## 🧩 Enhanced Master Prompt (paste this to the AI)

```
ROLE: Expert Full-Stack Developer and UI/UX Architect working inside the existing
SHEscale codebase — NOT a standalone feature. You already have full context of the
SHEscale architecture spec, the existing backend folder structure, the existing
Mongoose models, and the existing white + #F50A70 frontend design system.

TASK: Build the "Smart Scheme Matcher & Loan Application Generator" as an extension
of the already-planned Funding Hub Scheme Matcher feature (Feature 1.1 in the spec) —
do not create a parallel/duplicate feature.

TECH STACK: React.js (frontend), Node.js + Express (backend, ES6 `import` only, no
`require()`), MongoDB + Mongoose (already-built models), Gemini API via the existing
shared `services/geminiService.js`, faiss-node as the retrieval engine inside the
existing `services/ragRetrievalService.js`.

OBJECTIVE: A user describes their business idea, triggers a scan, and the system
returns the genuinely matching government/financial schemes (ranked, typically 3+,
never artificially padded) with pros/cons per scheme, then generates a tailored,
formal loan application for any scheme she selects.

────────────────────────────────────────
1. DATA LAYER — REUSE, DON'T DUPLICATE
────────────────────────────────────────
- Use the EXISTING `GovernmentScheme` model as the source of truth for scheme data
  (already kept current by the Live Government Scheme sync job). Only add new fields
  to it if something here is genuinely missing (e.g. a `prosConsSummary` field) —
  do not create a separate `Scheme` collection.
- Use the EXISTING `FundingApplication` model to store generated loan applications
  (add fields for `generatedApplicationText`, `status: ["draft","submitted"]` if not
  already present) — do not create a separate `UserApplication` collection.
- Every schema change must be additive and backward-compatible with what's already
  wired to the Live Government Scheme Panel and RAG pipeline.

────────────────────────────────────────
2. BACKEND — FOLD INTO THE EXISTING SERVICE LAYER
────────────────────────────────────────
Route: POST /api/schemes/scan
  - Controller validates input only, then calls `ragRetrievalService.retrieveMatches()`.
  - Inside `ragRetrievalService.js`: use faiss-node to run similarity search against
    the vectorized `GovernmentScheme` corpus, return the top genuinely relevant
    matches (not a forced count).
  - Pass the retrieved context + user's business idea into `geminiService.js`,
    which formats the final response as strict JSON: scheme name, badge, pros[],
    cons[], matchScore.
  - Response: JSON array, length = however many real matches, sorted by matchScore.

Route: POST /api/schemes/generate-application
  - Accepts `schemeId` + `businessIdeaText`.
  - Controller calls a new `fundingService.generateApplication()` function, which
    builds a scheme-specific prompt and calls `geminiService.js` (same shared
    wrapper, not a separate direct API call).
  - Persists the result to the EXISTING `FundingApplication` document for that user
    (create if none exists for this scheme, update otherwise).
  - Response: the generated application text + the saved application's ID.

Keep both routes thin — all prompt construction, retrieval logic, and formatting
lives in services, matching the rest of the SHEscale backend.

────────────────────────────────────────
3. FRONTEND — NEST UNDER THE EXISTING SCHEMEMATCHER SCREEN
────────────────────────────────────────
This feature lives INSIDE the already-planned `SchemeMatcher.jsx` screen in the
Funding Hub, built from these child components:

- `IdeaInput.jsx`
  - Spacious textarea + optional "attach business plan" selector + a primary CTA
    styled with the #F50A70 accent token (`--accent`), not a raw Tailwind color.
  - Real loading state (skeleton, not spinner-only) while the scan request is in flight.
  - Real empty state copy if the user hasn't scanned yet, real error state if the
    API call fails — no fake "no data" placeholder.

- `SchemeCards.jsx`
  - Renders one card per REAL match returned by the API (not a hardcoded 3) —
    ranked by matchScore, badge for the scheme name.
  - Pros/cons rendered with the same green-check / red-alert visual language
    already used in the PDF Doc-Whisperer, for platform-wide consistency —
    not a one-off icon set.
  - "Generate Loan Application" button per card, disabled + loading state while
    that specific card's generation request is in flight (don't lock the whole screen).

- `ApplicationDraft.jsx`
  - Modal/side-drawer showing the real generated text once the API responds.
  - "Save to Dashboard" persists to the real FundingApplication record (already
    done server-side on generation — this button can just confirm/navigate).
  - "Download PDF" triggers a real PDF export of the generated text.

All three components pull colors, spacing, and type scale from the SAME design
token file already defined for the rest of SHEscale — do not redefine styles locally.

────────────────────────────────────────
4. CODE QUALITY
────────────────────────────────────────
- ES6 `import` syntax only, across frontend and backend.
- Centralized `asyncHandler` + shared error-handling middleware — no repeated
  try/catch blocks per controller.
- Use the existing centralized API client (`services/api.js`) on the frontend —
  no inline fetch calls inside components.
- No mocked/sample data anywhere — every state (loading/empty/error/success) must
  reflect a real API response.

────────────────────────────────────────
5. OUTPUT FORMAT
────────────────────────────────────────
Output in this order: (1) any additive schema changes to the existing models,
(2) the two backend routes + their controllers, (3) the service functions inside
ragRetrievalService.js, geminiService.js, and fundingService.js, (4) the three
frontend components, (5) a short note confirming no new/duplicate collections
were created and the design tokens were reused, not redefined.
```

